Oh, yeah, sure, right. Add one more to the list of stupid pointless
unavoidable deaths. There I was, on level 23, debating whether I
should go up and muck around the upper levels looking for another
floating eye to get my lost telepathy back. I decided to rough it --
I'd just put on a blindfold each time I walked into a room, and apply
my mirror whenever anything got near me. If the mirror didn't kill it,
the sword would.

So I put on my levitation boots, and headed across the moat. And here
come the electric eels... No problem. Until I get the message...

  The electric eel drowns you -- More --
  Do you want your possessions identified?

ARRGH! Wimpy bloody eels can drown me? I had my levitation boots on, I
had teleportation, I figured I didn't have to worry about drowning.
But no...

I hadn't lost any hit points. And look at these attributes...

Final Attributes:

You were the Envoy of Balance.
You were piously aligned.
You could teleport.
You had teleport control.
You saw invisible.
You were fast.
You were stealthy.
You were poison resistant.
You were fire resistant.
You were cold resistant.
You were sleep resistant.
You had polymorph control.
You were warned.
You were protected.
You had reflection.
You were levitating.
You were displaced.
You were extremely lucky.
You had extra luck.
Good luck did not time out for you.

Interestingly enough, here's the scoreboard results:

